One thing to keep in mind when working with shiny is that is any data loaded on per session basis will allocate memory when each user connects. By default applications running are limited to 1GB of memory. If your application works fine with 1 user, but fails when the second user connects, it could be you are running out of memory. If this is happening, a message should be in your application logs.

