Great, thanks!

On Monday, June 11, 2018 at 10:41:26 AM UTC-4, Joshua Spiewak wrote:
> Thanks for reporting this. This is a regression when we shifted the base system to Xenial the other week. We are working on a fix.
>
> On Saturday, June 9, 2018 at 7:26:52 AM UTC-5, Wylie Timmerman wrote:
> > A recommendation (/question to confirm I'm not missing something):
> >
> > I recently found that a download button on my shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> Shiny app that provided a zip file no longer worked. After a whole lot of debugging, I found that R_ZIPCMD is not (or no longer?) set by default on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>. Could RStudio make the zip and unzip tools at R_ZIPCMD and R_UNZIPCMD available by default on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> apps? Or did I just mess something up?
> >
> > This issue was particularly nettlesome because zipping a subdirectory of my app folder created an error that took a while to trace to the zip function ("sh: 1: : Permission denied") and that appeared only server-side (I'm working on Windows 10 otherwise). For a reproducible example, my app folder contains app.R (below) and a subfolder called "Exports" with a few dummy files (another.csv, dfname.csv,export1.csv, export2.csv,readme.txt in this case, though they're not explicitly referenced) (though I'd normally create these through a script, I wanted to isolate any folder or file creation issues from the zipping issue). Pressing "getdata" works locally, but not on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>.
> >
> >  library(shiny)
> > library(tidyverse)
> >
> >
> > ui <- fluidPage(
> >   # Wrap the button in the function `withBusyIndicatorUI()`
> >   actionButton("run","Run me"),
> >   downloadButton(
> >     "downloadShp",
> >     "getdata")
> > )
> >
> >
> > server <- function(input, output, session) {
> >   print(getwd())
> >   print(list.files(getwd()))
> >   print(list.dirs(getwd()))
> >   print(list.files(file.path(getwd(),"Exports"),full.names = TRUE))
> >   print(Sys.info())
> >   print(sessionInfo())
> >   print(Sys.getenv())
> >
> >
> >   output$downloadShp <- downloadHandler(
> >     filename = function() {paste0("dltest.zip")},
> >     content = function(file) {
> >
> >       ziphere = dir("Exports",full.names = TRUE)
> >       print(ziphere)
> >
> >       return(zip(zipfile = file,
> >                  files = ziphere))
> >     },
> >     contentType = "application/zip"
> >   )#end of download shp
> >
> >   session$onSessionEnded(function() {
> >
> >
> >   })
> > }
> >
> >
> > shinyApp(ui = ui, server = server)
> >
> > What's a little challenging is that when zipping the Exports subfolder, the error returned is "sh: 1: : Permission denied", not something about not having zip tools at hand. For context, these are the logs, including lots of printouts on what files are present, SessionInfo, and Sys.getenv() results:
